# A global gitignore carrying Rust's "target/" (as ~/.gitignore_global does on
# at least one machine here) shadows OpenWrt's target/ source tree. Already
# tracked files are unaffected, but a NEW file under target/ is then silently
# refused by git add -- which loses board-support files. Re-include the
# directory; the more specific rule below still excludes the feeds symlinks.
!/target/
/target/linux/feeds
/overlay
/package/feeds
/package/openwrt-packages
/*.patch
/llvm-bpf*
key-build*
private-key.pem
public-key.pem
*.orig
*.rej
*~
.#*
*#
.emacs.desktop*
TAGS*~
git-src
.project
.cproject
.ccache
.vscode*
